---
title: Introduction
description: Formsnap wires Superforms data into accessible form markup — labels, controls, descriptions and errors that connect themselves.
---

<script>
	import { Callout } from "$lib/markdown";
</script>

Formsnap is a Svelte 5 component library that sits between [Superforms](https://superforms.rocks) and your markup. Superforms validates and owns your form data; Formsnap turns that data into correctly associated labels, inputs, descriptions and error messages.

```svelte title="settings-form.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Control, Field, Label } from "@emmorts/formsnap";

	let { form, formData } = $props();
</script>

<Field {form} name="email" fieldErrors>
	<Control>
		{#snippet children({ props })}
			<Label>Email</Label>
			<input type="email" {...props} bind:value={$formData.email} />
		{/snippet}
	</Control>
	{#snippet description()}We'll email you about your account.{/snippet}
</Field>
```

## Why Formsnap

- **Accessible by default.** Every control gets `id`/`name`, its label is associated, and descriptions plus errors are referenced through `aria-describedby` — only while they exist.
- **Type-safe paths.** Field names are checked against your schema's type, so a renamed property is a compile error, not a silent runtime miss.
- **Server-rendering safe.** Generated IDs are stable between SSR and hydration; nothing backpatches the DOM after the fact.
- **Unstyled and composable.** You own every element and class. Render props hand you the wiring, never the markup.

## Requirements

| Dependency             | Supported range                              |
| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| `svelte`               | `^5.30.2`                                    |
| `sveltekit-superforms` | `^2.19.0` or `^3.0.0`                        |
| schema library         | any Superforms adapter; the docs use zod v3  |

<Callout type="note">

Superforms 3 additionally requires Svelte `^5.56.4`. With Superforms 2.31+, import zod from `zod/v3` so the adapter types line up, and keep a single zod copy in your dependency tree (`pnpm why zod` to check).

</Callout>

